  "notes": "Rayleigh tests use pit centroid y (map metres). A globally incoherent ripple (phase drift across the window) can defeat the global phase test while still producing the local band-trough association; the two tests are complementary. The raw-DEM band at a pit centre contains the pit's own depression (which has power at the band wavelengths), so trough fractions from the raw DEM overstate the banding association for deep pits; the fill-DEM variant removes that leakage."
